Conflicts: honk
Replaces: honk
Description: eBPF transparent proxy engine (dae syntax, doona web UI)
 honk is an experimental transparent proxy for Linux written in Rust. It
 follows dae's eBPF datapath and configuration syntax and sing-box's outbound
 groups and Clash API, steering LAN-forwarded and host-originated TCP/UDP
 through TC eBPF. It speaks SOCKS5, Shadowsocks/2022, Trojan, AnyTLS,
 Hysteria2, TUIC, Juicity, VMess and VLESS (REALITY, Vision), with
 subscriptions, DNS routing and selector/urltest/fallback/score groups.
 .
 This package installs the official upstream "full" release unmodified: a
 static musl binary with the embedded doona web UI, the Clash-compatible and
 native APIs, plus honk-core.service. Upstream calls it early alpha. It needs
 Linux 6.12 or newer with BTF, cgroup v2 and bpffs.
